==English==
[[File:Pereza (Bradypus tridactylus) La Boyera, Miranda - Venezuela 000.jpg|right|thumb|An '''ai''' ({{taxfmt|Bradypus tridactylus|species}})]]

===Etymology 1===
Originated 1685–95, from {{bor|en|pt-BR|aí<id:sloth>}}, from {{der|en|tpw|a'y}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɑ.i/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-ai (sloth).oga|Audio (US)}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|s|*}}

# A [[pale-throated sloth]] ({{taxfmt|Bradypus tridactylus|species}}), endemic to forests of southern Venezuela, the Guianas, and northern Brazil.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|''Bradypus tridactylus''}} {{vern|maned sloth}}

====See also====
* {{l|en|unau}} ([[Linnaeus's two-toed sloth]] ({{taxfmt|Choloepus didactylus|species}}) or {{vern|Hoffmann's two-toed sloth}} ({{taxfmt|Choloepus hoffmanni|species}}))

====References====
* {{R:American Heritage 2000|ai}}
* {{R:Dictionary.com|ai}}

====Further reading====
* {{pedia}}
* {{specieslite|Bradypus tridactylus|i=1}}

===Etymology 2===
Contraction of {{m|en|aight}} (which itself is a contraction of {{m|en|all right}}).

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|aii}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/aɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-eye.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|ay|aye|I|eye}}

====Contraction====
{{en-head|contr}}

# {{lb|en|slang|US}} [[all right|All right]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Ai''', let's go.}}

